WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.088 --> 00:00:02.671
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.866 --> 00:00:08.082
- [Narrator] Romain Lacombe
is a man on a mission.

00:00:08.082 --> 00:00:09.673
- Air pollution is an environmental issue,

00:00:09.673 --> 00:00:12.184
but most of all it's a health crisis.

00:00:12.184 --> 00:00:15.100
- [Narrator] More than five
million people die every year

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.933
from pollution-related illnesses.

00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:20.228
Romain wants to change that.

00:00:20.228 --> 00:00:22.360
He has designed a system to help humans

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:24.954
learn more about the air they breathe

00:00:24.954 --> 00:00:29.344
and he did it in the most
unconventional way imaginable,

00:00:29.344 --> 00:00:31.991
using pigeons wearing tiny backpacks.

00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:36.158
- I will never look at pigeons
ever again like I did before.

00:00:37.158 --> 00:00:39.825
(upbeat music)

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.842
- [Narrator] London, like
many cities, has a problem,

00:00:47.842 --> 00:00:48.675
pollution.

00:00:49.688 --> 00:00:53.855
It's so bad here it kills
nearly 10,000 citizens a year.

00:00:56.663 --> 00:00:58.682
- The problem about the
weather and pollution

00:00:58.682 --> 00:00:59.913
is they interact together

00:00:59.913 --> 00:01:03.057
and sometimes create episodes
of very high pollution.

00:01:03.057 --> 00:01:05.224
- [Narrator] London weather
is notoriously fickle

00:01:05.224 --> 00:01:08.013
and pollution levels
change with the weather.

00:01:08.013 --> 00:01:12.180
Rains wash up pollutants
and winds sweep them away.

00:01:13.362 --> 00:01:17.185
Romain wanted to make
the invisible, visible.

00:01:17.185 --> 00:01:19.959
To do that, he found a
way for people to know

00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:23.134
when the air is particularly toxic.

00:01:23.134 --> 00:01:25.541
Enter the Pigeon Air Patrol.

00:01:25.541 --> 00:01:27.739
(upbeat music)

00:01:27.739 --> 00:01:28.872
- [Romain] The Pigeon Air Patrol

00:01:28.872 --> 00:01:30.680
was this brilliant, crazy idea

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:33.927
to fly a flock of pigeons
over the city of London

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:37.314
with tiny little backpacks
to measure air pollution.

00:01:37.314 --> 00:01:39.875
- [Narrator] Romain outfitted
a flock of ten birds

00:01:39.875 --> 00:01:43.578
to fly around London to monitor
air quality in real time.

00:01:43.578 --> 00:01:45.161
(upbeat music)

00:01:45.161 --> 00:01:47.911
(pigeons cooing)

00:01:49.288 --> 00:01:51.927
They wore special backpacks
equipped with sensors

00:01:51.927 --> 00:01:56.369
to measure pollutants like
ozone and nitrogen dioxide,

00:01:56.369 --> 00:01:58.715
and they weren't just ordinary birds,

00:01:58.715 --> 00:02:01.345
they were highly trained racing pigeons.

00:02:01.345 --> 00:02:04.364
- [Romain] We worked with
Brian, expert pigeon fancier

00:02:04.364 --> 00:02:06.816
who's been very widely
recognized in that field.

00:02:06.816 --> 00:02:08.377
These are professional pigeons.

00:02:08.377 --> 00:02:09.210
They race,

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:12.200
they know how to always home
back to their home base.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.254
We had an entire patrol of pigeons,

00:02:14.254 --> 00:02:16.563
Coco, Norbert, Julius ...

00:02:16.563 --> 00:02:19.146
(upbeat music)

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:30.555
- [Narrator] When the
pigeons took the to sky,

00:02:30.555 --> 00:02:33.129
the data they collected
was instantly accessible

00:02:33.129 --> 00:02:34.714
to anyone on the ground.

00:02:34.714 --> 00:02:37.544
Citizens could tweet the Pigeon Air Patrol

00:02:37.544 --> 00:02:39.074
and the nearest backpack sensor

00:02:39.074 --> 00:02:43.074
would respond with readings
from low to extreme.

00:02:43.946 --> 00:02:45.238
- Thanks to this, people tuned in

00:02:45.238 --> 00:02:47.455
to know when's a good time to go running

00:02:47.455 --> 00:02:50.088
and when you can bike without
worrying about pollution,

00:02:50.088 --> 00:02:52.199
or when you should really take extra care

00:02:52.199 --> 00:02:54.408
about the air you breathe.

00:02:54.408 --> 00:02:56.154
The Pigeon Air Patrol was
just a starting point,

00:02:56.154 --> 00:02:57.745
so of course the Pigeon Air Patrol

00:02:57.745 --> 00:02:59.607
was not fixing pollution in London,

00:02:59.607 --> 00:03:03.351
but by bringing attention from
everyone about this topic,

00:03:03.351 --> 00:03:06.060
we make it easier for
citizens to demand change.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:07.694
And so we make it easier
for everyone involved

00:03:07.694 --> 00:03:09.147
to say there's an issue there.

00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:10.175
We should recognize it,

00:03:10.175 --> 00:03:11.008
we should address it,

00:03:11.008 --> 00:03:11.841
and then we can fix it.

00:03:11.841 --> 00:03:14.424
(upbeat music)

